# Compass module endpoints (Phase 49 walking skeleton).
# Default port 5009 is for local `dotnet run` (launchSettings.json).
# Docker Compose uses port 5000 -- change @baseUrl if running via `make dev`.
#
# Auth: In Development mode, DevBypassMiddleware auto-authenticates as superadmin.
# NOTE: the default dev profile holds the nine TIMESHEET privileges, which grant NOTHING in
# Compass -- Compass inherits nothing, deliberately. Expect 403 unless you supply a Compass role.
# Use X-Dev-Roles to hold a Compass role instead.
#
# The identifier is a Guid: the directory record's primary key is a preserved uuid, and the route
# constraint is {id:guid}, so a non-Guid segment 404s at route binding.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5009

### Read one employee through the Compass directory boundary (needs a Compass role)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/v1/employees/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
X-Dev-Roles: Compass Admin

### Same request as a Compass root (the Compass-internal root satisfies the admin policy)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/v1/employees/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
X-Dev-Roles: Compass Super Admin

### Expect 403 -- a timesheet SuperAdmin is NOT a Compass user
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/v1/employees/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
X-Dev-Roles: SuperAdmin

### Expect 404 -- non-Guid segment fails route binding before the handler
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/v1/employees/not-a-guid
X-Dev-Roles: Compass Admin
